            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0198" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3703: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva (Gilbert) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-29T14:00:00+01:00">January 29, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 29—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. I have orally delivered to Cecil the communication conveyed in your 30,
                    January 28, noon.</p>
                <pb facs="0199" n="95" xml:id="pg95"/>
                <p>He wishes me to express to you his deep personal gratitude for your message. He
                    added, as his personal opinion, that the events at Shanghai had produced a
                    situation which called for immediate and strong action and that if such action
                    were not taken still worse troubles would develop.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
